rns once."},{"sids":["kernel/vmcore_info.c::PAGE_SLAB_MAPCOUNT_VALUE","kernel/vmcore_info.c::PAGE_BUDDY_MAPCOUNT_VALUE","kernel/vmcore_info.c::PAGE_HUGETLB_MAPCOUNT_VALUE","kernel/vmcore_info.c::PAGE_OFFLINE_MAPCOUNT_VALUE","kernel/vmcore_info.c::PAGE_UNACCEPTED_MAPCOUNT_VALUE","kernel/workqueue.c::__queue_delayed_work"],"text":"Page mapcount high byte tags slab, buddy, huge, offline and unaccepted; delayed path uses unbound CPU and pending-bit names."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["kernel/vhost_task.c::vhost_task_create","kernel/vmcore_info.c::hwerr_log_error_type"],"text":"Vhost creation shares filesystem, address, threads and signals untraced, inits completion and mutex first; hwerr ignores out-of-range source."},{"sids":["kernel/watch_queue.c::filter_watch_notification","kernel/watch_queue.c::watch_queue_pipe_buf_try_steal"],"text":"Notification passes only if type enabled and a rule matches subtype and masked info; watch pipe buffers forbid steal."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::pool_workqueue","kernel/workqueue.c::workqueue_struct","kernel/workqueue.c::wq_flusher"],"text":"Excess work parks on inactive list outside active tally; colors advance with flight tallies; plugged pauses dispatch."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::worker_pool_flags","kernel/workqueue.c::worker_pool","kernel/workqueue.c::manage_workers"],"text":"Associated pools bind workers with concurrency management; disassociated and BH pools run unbound; manager flag elects one manager."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::__queue_delayed_work","kernel/workqueue.c::send_mayday","kernel/workqueue.c::pool_mayday_timeout","kernel/workqueue.c::assign_rescuer_work"],"text":"Zero delay queues immediately; nonzero arms timer with housekeeping preference; mayday pins distressed queues for rescuer drain."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::alloc_node_nr_active","kernel/workqueue.c::rcu_free_wq","kernel/workqueue.c::rcu_free_pool"],"text":"Per-node accounting caps work via max, tally and pending list plus fallback; queue and pool free defers via RCU."}],"locks":[{"sids":["kernel/vhost_task.c::vhost_task_fn","kernel/vhost_task.c::vhost_task_stop"],"text":"Exit mutex serializes stop against signal-driven kill so one termination wins and kill handler cannot run after orderly stop began."},{"sids":["kernel/watch_queue.c::lock_wqueue","kernel/watch_queue.c::unlock_wqueue","kernel/watch_queue.c::add_watch_to_object","kernel/watch_queue.c::remove_watch_from_object"],"text":"Queue spinlock is BH-protected and fails if detached; add nests list lock inside, removal drops queue lock first."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::worker_pool","kernel/workqueue.c::pool_workqueue","kernel/workqueue.c::wq_pool_mutex","kernel/workqueue.c::workqueue_struct"],"text":"Pool lock covers flags, lists, timers, hashes, colors and tallies; global mutex guards registry; queue mutex guards colors and flushers."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::send_mayday","kernel/workqueue.c::pool_mayday_timeout","kernel/workqueue.c::idle_cull_fn","kernel/workqueue.c::worker_detach_from_pool"],"text":"Mayday list takes mayday lock inside pool lock; cull takes attach mutex outside pool lock; detach clears under attach mutex."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::queue_delayed_work_on","kernel/workqueue.c::mod_delayed_work_on","kernel/workqueue.c::flush_delayed_work"],"text":"Delayed queue, modify and flush hold interrupts disabled across pending-bit and timer or queue updates."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F1"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p05","crown":"A","phase":"F4"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["kernel/vhost_task.c::vhost_task_fn","kernel/vhost_task.c::vhost_task_flags"],"text":"Vhost thread cycles signal check, stop check, delegated work and sleep; kill runs only when stop was not requested."},{"sids":["kernel/watch_queue.c::post_one_notification"],"text":"Posting publishes into free slot and wakes readers or, when full or slotless, marks loss on newest entry without adding data."},{"sids":["kernel/watch_queue.c::init_watch","kernel/watch_queue.c::put_watch","kernel/watch_queue.c::put_watch_queue"],"text":"Watches and queues use reference counts with RCU-delayed destruction; final queue release frees pages, bitmap, filter and descriptor."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::worker_flags","kernel/workqueue.c::wq_worker_running","kernel/workqueue.c::wq_worker_sleeping","kernel/workqueue.c::wq_worker_tick"],"text":"Worker flags gate running tally; tick adds CPU time and may elevate over-threshold workers to intensive."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::worker_thread","kernel/workqueue.c::rescuer_thread"],"text":"Worker exits on die else processes pool list then idles without lost wakeup; rescuer drains distress in bounded batches."}],"structs":[{"sids":["kernel/vhost_task.c::vhost_task"],"text":"Vhost descriptor groups two callbacks with owner data, exit completion, stop and killed flags, thread reference and termination mutex."},{"sids":["kernel/vmcore_info.c::vmcoreinfo_data","kernel/vmcore_info.c::vmcoreinfo_note","kernel/vmcore_info.c::hwerr_info"],"text":"Crash state holds data buffer, note pointer and hardware-error table pairing counter with timestamp."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::worker_pool","kernel/workqueue.c::pool_workqueue","kernel/workqueue.c::workqueue_struct"],"text":"Pool carries lock, cpu, lists, timers, hashes and attrs; per-pool queue carries colors and tallies; queue carries pwqs, colors and limits."},{"sids":["kernel/workqueue.c::wq_drain_dead_softirq_work","kernel/workqueue.c::wq_barrier"],"text":"Dead-CPU drain object pairs work item with target pool and completion; barrier pairs work item with completion and informatory task pointer."},{"sids":["kernel/watch_queue.c::WATCH_QUEUE_NOTE_SIZE","kernel/watch_queue.c::WATCH_QUEUE_NOTES_PER_PAGE","kernel/workqueue.c::worker_pool_flags","kernel/workqueue.c::worker_flags"],"text":"Note unit is 128 bytes;